Let's now verify the patch file creation. But before that, let me re-examine the err path change in spglib.c. There's a possibility that `spn_get_operations_with_site_tensors` on success may set `*permutations` and `*equiv_atoms`, but then later the caller `spgms_get_symmetry_with_site_tensors` frees `permutations`. Our err path frees `*permutations` when NULL — wait, on the success path, we don't go to err, so no issue. On error, we free. Good.

But wait: in `spgms_get_symmetry_with_site_tensors`, after `get_symmetry_with_site_tensors` succeeds, it does:
```
for (i = 0; i < magnetic_symmetry->size; i++) { ... }
size = magnetic_symmetry->size;
sym_free_magnetic_symmetry(magnetic_symmetry);
free(permutations);
...
```
It frees `permutations` (local). Good.

In `get_magnetic_dataset`, after success it calls `spn_get_idealized_cell(permutations, ...)` etc. and later frees permutations. Let's verify it frees permutations.

